Description: Pair close tags by a name key that ignores whitespace
 A close tag closed the current element only when its name was
 byte-identical, so "</{{element}}>" did not close "<{{ element }}>". The
 close tag token now carries its parts when the name holds a template. A
 close tag name ends where a template starts, as an open tag name does
 (EHP-04), so "</h{{ level }}>" closes "<h{{ level }}>". Names are compared
 by a key with whitespace and a trailing "/" removed
 and letters lower-cased, as a browser ignores "/" in "</div/>". Only a
 Tag can be closed this way: the Document has no name, and its empty key
 must not match the empty close tag "</>".
Author: Numiko
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Test: test/parser/parse-for-eslint.test.ts ("Twig as part of the markup structure"); "drops an empty close tag at the top of the document"
Last-Update: 2026-10-22
